# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0035317> (imaginal disc-derived wing hair organization)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "GOC:mtg_sensu") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11064425") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:12540853") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0035317> "A process that is carried out at the cellular level that results in the assembly, arrangement of constituent parts, or disassembly of an imaginal disc-derived wing hair. A wing hair is an actin-rich, polarized, non-sensory apical projection that protrudes from each of the approximately 30,000 wing epithelial cells. An example of this is found in Drosophila melanogaster.")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0035317> "wing hair organisation")
